I have built two fonts for X11 "version" of NetHack (3.1.2).  I have used a LOT
of ideas/designs from chrdata.dat, and chrdata3.dat (this one is really good).
Also some ideas/designs came from monsters.dat, and the original X11 font
nh10.bdf.  And a LOT of ideas/design, and fine-tunning and touch-ups from
myself.  I would like *NOT* to take any credit for the artwork/designs/ideas I
got from the other fonts.  I wish I knew the authors' names, to credit them.  I
suppose chrdata.dat and monsters.dat are created/copyright by the author of
chrhack (chrhac23.arj).  I don't have a slightest idea who made chrdata3.dat,
and inside nh10.bdf there's ``COPYRIGHT "Copyright 1989-1991 Network Computing
Devices, Inc."''.  Obvously whatever work I have added I would like to place in
public domain, free to use by anyone for any purpose.  So, if there's enough
demand for the fonts I made/assembled, I will post them here in either ascii
or uuencoded form (.bdf files are ascii).  The two fonts are almost the same,
except in one the walls of the dungeon are of medium thickness and are crooked
(kind of like in monsters.dat), and in the other the walls are thick, and made
out of stone/bricks (like in chrdata3.dat).  Although you might find both of
these fonts to be far from perfect, I feel that they are much better then the
one used bu X11 NetHack by default (nh10.{bdf,snf}).

--Leo.
PS: I spend a WHOLE NIGHT, and a good part of the day drawing, designing, and
tweaking the fonts.  I wish there was something better then xfed for editing
fonts.  xfed gets my lowest marks.  It's free nonetheless, and it works
(kinda).


